IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cdba-nouns`
IMPORT `cdba-calendar`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-definitions`
IMPORT `cdba-reg-eligibility`

-- Canada Disability Benefit Act (S.C. 2023, c. 17) -- the sections that decide something for a
-- person. Where the Act leaves a number, a condition or a date to the Regulations, the rule
-- takes it from the Canada Disability Benefit Regulations (SOR/2025-35), and says so.
--
-- Not in the text and therefore not carried as a value: the date of royal assent (the text
-- shows no assent date) and the day the Act came into force (s 14 leaves it to an order). Both
-- are stated inputs where a rule needs them.
--
-- The preamble, ss 1 to 3, 10, 11 to 13 are inert for a person; NOTES.md says why, one row each.

§ `Act s 4 -- Eligibility`

-- 4: a person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit if they meet the eligibility criteria
-- set out in the regulations. The Regulations set two sets of criteria: those for an
-- allocation, month by month (Regulations s 2), and those for the supplemental amount
-- (Regulations s 2.1).
-- src:38 | Eligibility
-- src:39 | 4 A person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit if they meet the eligibility criteria set out in the regulations.
@ref Act s 4 (src:38-39)
GIVEN facts IS A `Person facts for a month`
      `obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      payments IS A LIST OF `Payment made after a certificate`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` facts `obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` payments MEANS
        `the person is eligible to receive an allocation for the month` facts
     OR `a supplemental amount is owed for the certificate` `obtained a certificate referred to in paragraph 118.3(1)(a.2) or (a.3) of the Income Tax Act` payments

§ `Act s 5 -- Payment of benefit`

-- 5: the Minister must, in accordance with the regulations, pay a benefit to a person who is
-- eligible, applies or has an application made on their behalf in accordance with the
-- regulations, and meets any other conditions set out in the regulations. The rule says
-- when the Minister's duty has arisen; the Regulations (ss 4 to 9) say what is paid, and when.
-- src:40 | Payment of benefit
-- src:41 | 5 The Minister must, in accordance with the regulations, pay a Canada disability benefit to a person who is eligible for the benefit, applies or has an application made on their behalf, in accordance with the regulations, and meets any other conditions set out in the regulations.
@ref Act s 5 (src:40-41)
GIVEN `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person applies or an application is made on their behalf in accordance with the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person meets any other condition set out in the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must pay a Canada disability benefit to the person` `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit` `the person applies or an application is made on their behalf in accordance with the regulations` `the person meets any other condition set out in the regulations` MEANS
        `the person is eligible for a Canada disability benefit`
    AND `the person applies or an application is made on their behalf in accordance with the regulations`
    AND `the person meets any other condition set out in the regulations`

§ `Act s 6 -- Obligation to provide information`

-- 6: an applicant, or the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their
-- own affairs, must give the Minister any information the Minister may require in respect of the
-- application. The duty has arisen when the Minister requires the information.
-- src:44 | Obligation to provide information
-- src:45 | 6 An applicant or the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs must provide the Minister with any information that the Minister may require in respect of the application.
@ref Act s 6 (src:44-45)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister requires the information in respect of the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person must provide the Minister with the information` `the person is an applicant` `the person is the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs` `the Minister requires the information in respect of the application` MEANS
        (   `the person is an applicant`
         OR `the person is the representative of an applicant who is incapable of managing their own affairs`)
    AND `the Minister requires the information in respect of the application`

§ `Act s 7 -- Social Insurance Number`

-- 7: the Minister is authorized to collect and use an applicant's Social Insurance Number for
-- the purposes of administering and enforcing the Act.
-- src:46 | Social Insurance Number
-- src:47 | 7 The Minister is authorized to collect and use, for the purposes of the administration and enforcement of this Act, the Social Insurance Number of an applicant.
@ref Act s 7 (src:46-47)
GIVEN `the person is an applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister is authorized to collect and use the person's Social Insurance Number` `the person is an applicant` `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of the Act` MEANS
        `the person is an applicant`
    AND `the purpose is the administration or enforcement of the Act`

§ `Act s 8 -- Agreements`

-- 8(1): to carry out the purposes of the Act the Minister may make agreements with any
-- department or agency of the Government of Canada, and, with the Governor in Council's
-- approval, with any department or agency of a province. 8(2): the Minister must make public
-- any agreement entered into under 8(1).
-- src:48 | Agreements
-- src:49 | 8 (1) In order to carry out the purposes of this Act, the Minister may enter into agreements with any department or agency of the Government of Canada and may, with the approval of the Governor in Council, enter into agreements with any department or agency of a province.
-- src:50 | Publication
-- src:51 | (2) The Minister must make public any agreement entered into under subsection (1).
@ref Act s 8(1) and (2) (src:48-51)
GIVEN party IS A `Party to an agreement`
      `the Governor in Council has approved the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister may enter into an agreement with the party` party `the Governor in Council has approved the agreement` MEANS
    CONSIDER party
    WHEN `a department or agency of the Government of Canada` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a department or agency of a province`                THEN `the Governor in Council has approved the agreement`
    WHEN `anyone else`                                         THEN FALSE

@ref Act s 8(2) (src:51)
GIVEN `the agreement was entered into under subsection 8(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Minister must make the agreement public` `the agreement was entered into under subsection 8(1)` MEANS
    `the agreement was entered into under subsection 8(1)`

§ `Act s 9 -- Payments cannot be charged, etc.`

-- 9: how a benefit stands against each kind of claim the section names. Only the four kinds
-- the section names have an answer; for retention under this Act itself section 9(c) leaves the
-- benefit unshielded (it speaks only of Acts other than this one); for any other claim the
-- text does not say.
-- src:52 | Payments cannot be charged, etc.
-- src:53 | 9 A benefit under this Act
-- src:54 | (a) is not subject to the operation of any law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency;
-- src:55 | (b) cannot be assigned, charged, attached or given as security;
-- src:56 | (c) cannot be retained by way of deduction, set-off or compensation under any Act of Parliament other than this Act; and
-- src:57 | (d) is garnishable moneys for the purposes of the Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act.
@ref Act s 9 (src:52-57)
GIVEN claim IS A `Claim against a benefit`
GIVETH A `Position of a benefit against a claim`
`how the benefit stands against the claim` claim MEANS
    CONSIDER claim
    WHEN `an operation of a law relating to bankruptcy or insolvency` THEN `the benefit is shielded from the claim`
    WHEN `an assignment, charge, attachment or giving as security` THEN `the benefit is shielded from the claim`
    WHEN `a retention by deduction, set-off or compensation under an Act of Parliament other than the Act` THEN `the benefit is shielded from the claim`
    WHEN `a retention by deduction, set-off or compensation under the Act` THEN `section 9 does not shield the benefit from the claim`
    WHEN `a garnishment for the purposes of the Family Orders and Agreements Enforcement Assistance Act` THEN `the benefit is garnishable moneys`
    WHEN `any other claim` THEN `the text does not say`

§ `Act s 10.1 -- Appeals`

-- 10.1: subject to regulations, a person, or any other person acting on their behalf, may
-- appeal to the body the regulations identify in respect of any decision (a) relating to the
-- person's ineligibility, (b) relating to the amount of a benefit received or to be received,
-- or (c) prescribed by the regulations. Regulations ss 18 to 20 narrow this: see
-- `how the person may challenge the decision` in cdba-reg-appeals.l4.
-- src:60 | Appeals
-- src:61 | 10.1 Subject to regulations, a person, or any other person acting on their behalf, may appeal to a body identified in regulations made under paragraph 11(1)(i) in respect of any decision
-- src:62 | (a) relating to the person’s ineligibility for a Canada disability benefit;
-- src:63 | (b) relating to the amount of a Canada disability benefit that the person has received or will receive; or
-- src:64 | (c) prescribed by the regulations.
@ref Act s 10.1 (src:60-64)
GIVEN `the decision relates to the person's ineligibility for a Canada disability benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision relates to the amount of a Canada disability benefit that the person has received or will receive` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the decision is prescribed by the regulations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act allows an appeal in respect of the decision` `the decision relates to the person's ineligibility for a Canada disability benefit` `the decision relates to the amount of a Canada disability benefit that the person has received or will receive` `the decision is prescribed by the regulations` MEANS
        `the decision relates to the person's ineligibility for a Canada disability benefit`
     OR `the decision relates to the amount of a Canada disability benefit that the person has received or will receive`
     OR `the decision is prescribed by the regulations`

§ `Act s 14 -- Coming into force`

-- 14: the Act comes into force on a day fixed by order of the Governor in Council, but no later
-- than the first anniversary of the day it received royal assent. The assent date is not in the
-- text and the order is not in the text, so both days are inputs.
-- src:126 | Coming into Force
-- src:127 | Order in council or first anniversary
-- src:128 | 14 This Act comes into force on a day to be fixed by order of the Governor in Council, but no later than the first anniversary of the day on which it receives royal assent.
@ref Act s 14 (src:126-128)
GIVEN `the day the Act received royal assent` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest day on which the Act could be brought into force` `the day the Act received royal assent` MEANS
    `add years` `the day the Act received royal assent` 1

@ref Act s 14 (src:126-128)
GIVEN `the day the Act received royal assent` IS A DATE
      `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the day fixed for commencement is within the time section 14 allows` `the day the Act received royal assent` `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council` MEANS
    `the day fixed by order of the Governor in Council` AT MOST `the latest day on which the Act could be brought into force` `the day the Act received royal assent`
